# =============================================================================
# molaro_T-20_h1.00_79h_a1e-3_coarse.opts
#
# COARSE arm of the MESH-RESOLUTION PAIR, at a severely kinetics-limited
# alpha_c. Pair with geometry/molaro/molaro_2D_L387um_eps0.87um_axisym_T-20pair_tangent.opts
#
# THIS ARM: 631 x 198 (125k nodes), neck floor 60.1 um WIDTH -- does NOT resolve
#           Molaro's measured 32.8-64.8 um range
#
# THE QUESTION
# ------------
# Both arms are the same physics, the same grains, the same tangent contact;
# only eps differs. If they recover the SAME power law where they overlap,
# coarse meshes are adequate for the rest of the campaign and everything
# downstream gets ~13x cheaper. If they disagree, the neck-VISIBILITY criterion
# (the fillet rho ~ r^2/(2R) must exceed the ~6*eps diffuse band before the
# neck can be measured at all) is binding, and the fine mesh is mandatory.
#
# This is NOT the same as K&P's Eq. 45, which BOTH arms satisfy. Eq. 45 is
# asymptotic validity of the sharp-interface limit; visibility is whether the
# feature can be measured on the grid. The pair tests which one governs in
# practice, which is not something we can settle by argument.
#
# alpha_c = 1e-3, AND POINTWISE
# -----------------------------
# -alpha_pointwise 1 evaluates alpha_c at every quadrature point via
# AlphaCondensation() and rebuilds mob_sub and alph_sub from it through the
# M&F SI Eq. 9 bracket. -alpha_model 0 holds alpha_c constant at -alpha_c0, so
# this run exercises the pointwise MACHINERY without also varying alpha_c --
# T and rho_v still enter through rho_vs(T) and D_v(T), which main()'s scalars
# ignored entirely.
#
# 1e-3 is the bottom of the Braun et al. (2024) range, chosen to be SEVERELY
# kinetics-limited: L* = beta_HK*D_v = 139 um at -20 C against a neck radius of
# 15-30 um, so r/L* = 0.22. Kuczynski's r ~ t^(1/3) is derived in exactly this
# regime and Demmenie's experiments sit in it, which is the reason for taking
# the minimum rather than a middle value.
#
# -beta_sub0 IS IGNORED under -alpha_pointwise 1, since beta_sub is rebuilt
# from alpha_c pointwise. It is omitted here rather than left in to rot; the
# solver prints a banner if one is supplied anyway.
#
# t_final = 2.83e5 s (79 h). At alpha_c = 1e-3 the kinetics are ~13x slower
# than at the 1.34e-2 the earlier files used; t_final was scaled with the total
# resistance beta_sub + r/(D_v*chi) so the run still reaches a comparable neck.
#
# dtmax = 9.43e2 = min(1.1*tau_sub, t_final/300) with tau_sub = 5.9757e3 s. The
# 300-step floor matters here: tau_sub grows as 1/alpha_c, so the campaign's
# dtmax ~ 1.1*tau_sub rule alone would leave this arm with far too few steps to
# read a slope from.
#
# Measure: python postprocess/neck_width.py <run_dir> --axisym
# Fit:     python postprocess/fit_neck_growth.py <run>/neck_width.csv \
#              inputs/validation/molaro2019_fig11_T-20.csv --demmenie
# =============================================================================

-t_final 2.83e5                         # 79 h

-temp -20.0
-humidity 1.00
-grad_temp0 0.0,0.0,0.0

-alpha_pointwise 1                      # mob_sub/alph_sub per quadrature point
-alpha_model 0                          # constant alpha_c; isolates the machinery
-alpha_c0 1.0e-3                        # bottom of Braun's range -> kinetics-limited
-alpha_lo 1.0e-3
-alpha_hi 1.0e-1

-d0_sub0 1.0166e-9                      # physical capillary length at -20 C

-dtmax 9.43e2
-dtCFL 1
-dtCFL_dphimax 0.2

-t_out_log 80
-t_out_log_t0 1.0e2
